*** Resetting replication at the very beginning of the test.

*** Determining the first fresh binary log name.

*** Creating a simple table and filling it with some data.
CREATE TABLE t1(id INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT, PRIMARY KEY(id)) ENGINE=InnoDB;
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(DEFAULT);

*** Generating a configuration file in JSON format for the Binlog
*** Server utility.

*** Determining binlog file directory from the server.

*** Creating a temporary directory <BINSRV_STORAGE_PATH> for storing
*** binlog files downloaded via the Binlog Server utility.

*** Executing the Binlog Server utility to download all binlog data
*** from the server.

*** Making a copy of the first binlog metadata file

*** Inserting more data to the table.
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(DEFAULT);

*** Simulating temporary object presence in the storage.

*** Executing the Binlog Server utility to clean temporary objects and
*** to receive events generated by the second insert.

*** Checking that the Binlog Server utility removed temporary objects.
include/assert_grep.inc [Binlog storage initialization removed temporary objects ('found' message)]
include/assert_grep.inc [Binlog storage initialization removed temporary objects ('removed' message)]

*** Simulating corrupted storage state by replacing the first binlog
*** metadata file.

*** Executing the Binlog Server utility to initiate the recovery process.

*** Checking that the Binlog Server utility recovered the first binlog
*** file.
include/assert_grep.inc [Binlog storage initialization recovered the first binlog file]

*** Flushing the first binary log and switching to the second one.
FLUSH BINARY LOGS;

*** Dropping the table.
DROP TABLE t1;

*** Executing the Binlog Server utility one more time to receive missing
*** events from the first binlog.

*** Comparing server and downloaded versions of the first binlog file.

*** Simulating corrupted storage state by replacing the first binlog
*** metadata file which is not the latest one anymore.

*** Executing the Binlog Server utility to initiate the recovery process
*** but fail because the size mismatch is not in the latest binlog file.

*** Checking that the Binlog Server utility detected unrecoverable
*** storage corruption.
include/assert_grep.inc [Binlog storage initialization discovered unrecoverable state]

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility storage directory.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility log file.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility configuration file.
